<article class="env-corollary" id="E2060F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/E2060F">Corollary <span data-tag="E2060F">6.3.4.7</span>.</a> The $\infty $-category $\RGeom $ admits small limits. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Corollaries <a href="/tag/E1B861" data-tag="E1B861">4.2.3.11</a> and <a href="/tag/B67AE3" data-tag="B67AE3">4.4.2.4</a>, it suffices to show that $\RGeom $ admits filtered limits, a final object, and pullbacks. The existence of filtered limits follows from Theorem <a href="/tag/6C6B8D" data-tag="6C6B8D">6.3.3.1</a>, the existence of a final object follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/A780C6" data-tag="A780C6">6.3.4.1</a>, and the existence of pullbacks follows from Proposition <a href="/tag/11831D" data-tag="11831D">6.3.4.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>